Process note: pages were fetched via direct curl (with a browser User-Agent)
rather than the WebFetch tool, because WebFetch returned HTTP 429 (rate
limited) on the first batch of parallel calls. curl fetches succeeded with
HTTP 200 for all 37 URLs on the first attempt. Content was parsed with a
small custom Python HTML parser (stdlib only, no bs4 available in this
environment) restricted to the WordPress "post-content" article div for
headings/links/CTAs, and scanned across the full page for <img> tags (per
task instructions to capture "every image on the page").
